{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231405 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b3a1dcb-3788-58c3-9bf2-b0f681060ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of the Fourier Series For the Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe92f4fa-7615-54d2-a819-127fb1a673f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372862} {:answer/id #uuid "3b55cc73-4e32-591c-bee5-a9d934861abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372863} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b6aad-9479-5fcd-b841-a17705d991a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372864} {:answer/id #uuid "b3faa44a-d5ae-5692-901c-7fe9f2979668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b6aad-9479-5fcd-b841-a17705d991a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372864} :answer-field/id #uuid "f04ef90f-3003-58fb-a7fe-77d398fbdee2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f67e1f7-be25-5035-9c23-854e909c6a11" :question/math-academy-id "q-344268" :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}\\,y=f(x)\n$$\n\non $[-5,5]$, where $f$ is $10$-periodic and odd. Which Fourier-series form is appropriate for a particular solution ${y}_{p}?$\n\n$\\,$\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Because $f$ is $10$-periodic on $[-5,5]$, we have $L=5$, so Fourier series on this interval use the basis \n\n$$\ncos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\\,\\text{and}\\,sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNext, since $f$ is odd, its Fourier series contains only sine terms. For a second-order equation with no ${y}^{′}$ (damping) term, the particular solution inherits this property and is also an odd function.\n\nTherefore, the appropriate form for ${y}_{p}$ is a sine series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231405 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b3a1dcb-3788-58c3-9bf2-b0f681060ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of the Fourier Series For the Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417e9b86-46f1-5505-b2b8-827b75bf916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455013} {:answer/id #uuid "467d0a11-3d59-5056-8c67-302264331708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455021} {:answer/id #uuid "4d50a330-e973-52eb-b27c-39dd3a1bb1d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455038} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcb936a-b5c3-5867-a96a-a7f463d31cb9" :answer/ty